# Form field alignment

When creating or editing pages, **every control in the same row must be the same height and sit on the same baseline**. Dropdowns, text inputs, number inputs, and date widgets must not mix native heights.

## Required

- Use `--admin-control-height` (`38px`) for single-line inputs and selects
- Align row grids with `align-items: end` so labels can wrap without knocking controls off-line
- Style `<select>` with `appearance: none` and a matching chevron — never leave Safari’s taller native dropdown
- AU date widgets (`.au-date-input`) must match the same 38px height, padding, and radius as adjacent fields
- Checkboxes, radios, and textareas are the exception (they are not single-line row controls)

```css
/* ❌ BAD — native select taller than date/number beside it */
.featured-details-row { display: grid; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.featured-details-row { display: grid; align-items: end; }
.admin-field select,
.admin-field input:not([type="checkbox"]):not([type="radio"]) {
  height: var(--admin-control-height);
  min-height: var(--admin-control-height);
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```
